sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Actor
    participant C as Client
    participant I as Ingest
    participant E as Events
    participant T as Trigger
    participant G as Engine
    participant S as Score
    participant P as Public
    participant O as Overlay

    A->>C: Point, undo, reset, spectate or register
    alt Browser scoring action
        C->>E: addDoc(event with scoreVersion)
    else ESP32 device action
        C->>I: POST event
        I->>E: append event with server timestamp
    end

    E-->>T: Document created
    T->>T: Read court, event and score in transaction
    T->>T: Reject stale version or duplicate event
    alt Event is out of order or undo needs full history
        T->>G: Replay applicable event log
    else Normal scoring event
        T->>G: Apply event
    end
    G-->>T: Materialized score
    T->>S: Transactional update
    S-->>C: onSnapshot live score

    opt Public scoreboard or overlay
        O->>P: GET /r/{courtId}
        P->>S: Read current score
        P-->>O: Revision and score payload
        O->>P: GET /s or /m/{courtId}
        P->>E: Replay for stats or momentum
        P-->>O: Cached derived payload
    end

    opt Callable resetCourt
        C->>E: Archive and delete current events
        C->>S: Clear score/current
        C->>C: Increment court scoreVersion
    end

Note over G,S: Modes: standard, straight, tiebreakTen
Note over C,I: Device auth and replay hardening is a separate production requirement
